      "title": "STZ Q2 Earnings Call Highlights Improving Demand and Outlook",
      "summary": "Constellation Brands (STZ) reaffirmed its fiscal 2027 EPS guidance of $11.20-$11.90 during its Q2 earnings call, citing improving September beer demand, stronger marketing execution, and healthier distributor inventories. The company beat earnings expectations ($3.74 vs. $3.62 consensus) and revenue estimates ($2.63B vs. $2.57B consensus). While Pacifico and Victoria showed strong growth (20% and mid-teens respectively), Modelo and Corona faced headwinds. Management projects second-half beer margins of 34.5%-35.5% amid higher marketing costs and seasonal weakness.",
